[08:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'cinematic lighting. We generate, download the frame, and take it into Higgsfield. And here\'s the angle we got. &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; The camera\'s right above her now,'

[08:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'pressing down making her feel small in the frame. The exact opposite feel of that low angle just by moving where the camera sits. Now, a wide shot to show off the entire location. We click wide and the camera pulls all the way back. Still, both boxes ticked, we set our'

[08:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'camera move to pull out and keep our look/style to moody cinematic lighting. Then we generate, download the [music] frame, and back into Higgsfield one more time. And look how far back the camera lands. She\'s small in the frame now, the whole'

[09:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'neon street stretching out around her, exactly the wide we blocked. Now, here\'s the best part. We\'re not even these presets. If the exact angle we want isn\'t one of the buttons, we just guide the camera there ourselves and Let me show you with a clean side'

[09:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'profile. We rotate the subject with the rotate slider until we\'re looking straight at the left side. Then we drag the lens slider to zoom in a little and press E to lift the camera for a higher angle. With both boxes still ticked, we set our camera move to tracking and our'

[09:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'look/style to moody cinematic lighting. From here, we hit generate, download the frame, and into Higgsfield. And there\'s our side profile. The camera\'s locked dead on to the side,'

[09:51] [scene:talk]
